---
title: Sesame Miso Noodles
servings: 2
prep-time: 10 minutes
cook-time: 8 minutes
tags: [noodles, recipe, miso, sesame, asian-cuisine]
source: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DSLZUMWk8FZ/
image: https://scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/588410847_17931000477151947_2095614537801016614_n.jpg?stp=cmp1_dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=tFUnogodwi8Q7kNvwHbJHB4&_nc_oc=Adn2GEn7fjhukCDHwNH169JmSFouC-0XyDzA_yyyW0zijDsUeaObDyT31yDVVYLgRUI&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=WqnD07mqcFNpTwxfTU_t3A&oh=00_AflG5Jo14ar_Y_Lwv2uExD4xVbYuTwINFLa_oJX1Za0DUw&oe=6957847A
---

Bring a pot of water to a boil and cook @momofuku refined noodles{8%oz} until al dente, ~{4%minutes}.

In a bowl, whisk together @white miso paste{2%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @honey{1%tsp}, @rice vinegar{1%tsp}, @sesame oil{1%tsp}, @garlic{1%clove}, @ginger{1%tsp}, and @sriracha{1%tsp} until smooth.

Drain the noodles and add them to the bowl with the sauce, tossing until well coated, ~{1%minutes}.

Finish with @sesame seeds{1%tbsp} and @scallions{2%stalks}, then serve immediately.